---
import { withBase } from '../../lib/paths';

// Still frames from the arena renderer, all on the right paddle's view of seed 4, tick 8.
const players = [
  {
    id: 'fable',
    name: 'Fable 5.2',
    logo: 'anthropic.svg',
    edges: [78, 222],
    moves: ['Down', 'Down'],
  },
  {
    id: 'astra',
    name: 'Astra 6.2',
    logo: 'openai.svg',
    edges: [129, 164],
    moves: ['Hold', 'Down'],
  },
  {
    id: 'gemini',
    name: 'Gemini Neon',
    logo: 'gemini.png',
    edges: [127, 127],
    moves: ['Down', 'Hold'],
  },
  {
    id: 'grok',
    name: 'Grok 4.7 Heavy',
    logo: 'grok.jpg',
    edges: [30, 36],
    moves: ['Up', 'Down'],
  },
];
---

<figure
  class="network-sheet"
  aria-label="Four Pong players before and after revision"
>
  <div class="players">
    {
      players.map((player) => (
        <div class="pair">
          <div class="name">
            <img
              src={withBase('/experiments/pong/arena/logos/' + player.logo)}
              alt=""
              width="20"
              height="20"
            />
            {player.name}
          </div>
          {['Original', 'Revised'].map((version, i) => (
            <div class="snapshot">
              <a
                class="version"
                download
                aria-label={
                  'Download ' + player.name + ' ' + version + ' weights'
                }
                href={withBase(
                  '/experiments/pong/arena/players/' +
                    player.id +
                    '-' +
                    version.toLowerCase() +
                    '.json',
                )}
              >
                {version} ↓
              </a>
              <img
                src={withBase(
                  '/images/weight-space-pong/' +
                    player.id +
                    '-' +
                    version.toLowerCase() +
                    '.webp',
                )}
                width="620"
                height="568"
                loading="lazy"
                decoding="async"
                alt={
                  player.name +
                  ' ' +
                  version +
                  ' network with ' +
                  player.edges[i] +
                  ' nonzero connections. Selected move: ' +
                  player.moves[i].toLowerCase() +
                  '.'
                }
              />
              <div class="reading">
                {player.edges[i]} connections · {player.moves[i]}
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    All eight networks see the same ball and paddles. Read each picture from the
    six inputs on the left through the two middle layers to the three moves on
    the right. Lines show nonzero connection weights. Brightness shows the size
    of a node’s response relative to others in its layer. The ring marks the
    chosen move. Select Original or Revised to download that player’s weights.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
<style>
  .network-sheet {
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }
  .players {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 20rem), 1fr));
    gap: 1px;
    background: #465052;
    padding: 1px;
  }
  .pair {
    background: #101416;
    color: #f1f3f2;
    display: grid;
    align-content: start;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    padding: 0.75rem;
    gap: 0.4rem 0.5rem;
  }
  .name {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    font-weight: 650;
  }
  .network-sheet img {
    filter: none;
  }
  .name img {
    width: 20px;
    height: 20px;
    object-fit: contain;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .snapshot {
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .snapshot img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .version,
  .reading {
    color: #ccd4d5;
    font:
      0.76rem/1.45 ui-monospace,
      monospace;
  }
  figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.7rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
</style>
